<article class="env-lemma" id="0GVU">
  <p><a class="environment-identifier" href="/tag/0GVU">Lemma <span data-tag="0GVU">87.37.5</span>.</a> Let $S$ be a scheme. Let $X$ be a formal algebraic space over $S$. Let $T \subset |X_{red}|$ be a closed subset. The reduction $(X_{/T})_{red}$ of the completion $X_{/T}$ of $X$ along $T$ is the reduced induced closed subspace $Z$ of $X_{red}$ corresponding to $T$. </p>
</article><article class="env-proof">
    <p>
      <strong>Proof.</strong>
      It follows from Lemma <a href="/tag/0AIN" data-tag="0AIN">87.12.1</a>, Properties of Spaces, Definition <a href="/tag/047X" data-tag="047X">66.12.5</a> (which uses Properties of Spaces, Lemma <a href="/tag/03IQ" data-tag="03IQ">66.12.3</a> to construct $Z$), and the definition of $X_{/T}$ that $Z$ and $(X_{/T})_{red}$ are reduced algebraic spaces characterized the same mapping property: a morphism $g : Y \to X$ whose source is a reduced algebraic space factors through them if and only if $|Y|$ maps into $T \subset |X|$. 
      <span class="qed">$\square$</span>
    </p>
</article>